   "e26": {
    "color": "white",
    "h": 110,
    "kind": "rounded",
    "size": "small",
    "text": "**Today, in the portal:** the things tree and the ⌘K index are read from the model (`nav.ts`), but the five rail panels, their fixed pages and every route are written by hand (`nav.ts`, `route.ts`). Plugged In has no map at all. UI SDK has menus, navigation, a command palette, a tree and collapsibles, but no sidebar, breadcrumb, shell or router.",
    "textAlign": "left",
    "type": "shape",
    "w": 900,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 620
   },
   "e30": {
    "color": "green",
    "h": 220,
    "kind": "rounded",
    "size": "small",
    "text": "**What falls out**\n- the router, and a typed link to every page\n- the sidebar and its groups\n- the breadcrumb, from routes and their params\n- the palette: what you may open and call here\n- the agent's map: where it can go, what it can do\n- a docs page per screen, and journeys through pages in prove\n- a stale mark on your page code when its operations change",
    "textAlign": "left",
